Android's desktop audio HAL requests two capture periods, with 3840 or 7680
bytes per period at 48 kHz stereo S32_LE. Renoir advertises exactly four
periods and a 4096-byte minimum, rejecting those configurations.

Allow two periods and use the generic upstream ACP driver's 1024-byte
minimum. Keep the existing maxima and fixed DMA allocation; Renoir already
programs its ring size and interrupt watermark from negotiated parameters.
This is a Renoir compatibility candidate, not a generic ACP driver switch.
Drop when upstream Renoir accepts these buffers or a verified upstream ACP
replacement makes this driver unnecessary.

--- a/sound/soc/amd/renoir/rn_acp3x.h
+++ b/sound/soc/amd/renoir/rn_acp3x.h
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
-#define CAPTURE_MIN_NUM_PERIODS     4
+#define CAPTURE_MIN_NUM_PERIODS     2
 #define CAPTURE_MAX_NUM_PERIODS     4
 #define CAPTURE_MAX_PERIOD_SIZE     8192
-#define CAPTURE_MIN_PERIOD_SIZE     4096
+#define CAPTURE_MIN_PERIOD_SIZE     1024
 
 #define MAX_BUFFER (CAPTURE_MAX_PERIOD_SIZE * CAPTURE_MAX_NUM_PERIODS)
 #define MIN_BUFFER MAX_BUFFER
